==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*süü}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*süxe}} or {{m|urj-pro|*süje}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|süü}}, {{cog|kpv|си}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[fibre]]
#: {{syn|fi|kuitu}}
# [[filament]]
# {{lb|fi|usually|in plural}} [[grain]] {{gloss|linear texture of a material or surface}}
#: {{ux|fi|Koivun '''syyt''' ovat yleensä suorat.|The '''grain''' of birch is usually straight.}}
# [[reason]]
#: {{ux|fi|'''Syy''' tähän on...|The '''reason''' for this is...}}
#: {{ux|fi|On '''syytä''' tietää, että...|It is '''worth''' knowing that... (literally: There is a '''reason''' to know that...)}}
# [[fault]] {{gloss|blame; responsibility for a mistake}}
#: {{ux|fi|Se on sinun '''syytäsi'''.|It is your '''fault'''.}}

